>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="back-boilers">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Still got a back boiler in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">We do not service back boilers. We take them out, cap the gas fire in front, and fit a new combi boiler in their place.</p>
      <p>St Helens still has a lot of back boilers. Many WA10 and WA9 Victorian terraces run their heating from a boiler behind the gas fire in the front room. Most of these are now old, and parts are hard to find.</p>
      <h3>Why are back boilers a worry?</h3>
      <p>A back boiler sits inside the chimney breast. It has an open flue, so it relies on the chimney to draw fumes up and out. If the chimney gets part blocked, or the boiler cracks, fumes can spill into the room. That includes carbon monoxide. You cannot see it or smell it.</p>
      <h3>What we do instead</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>We remove the old back boiler.</li>
        <li>We disconnect and safely cap the gas fire.</li>
        <li>We fit a new combi boiler in a place that suits you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See <a href="/boiler-installation-st-helens">boiler installation in St Helens</a> for fixed-price packages from £2,195 fitted.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Got a gas fire but no back boiler?</strong> We do not service gas fires. We can disconnect and cap one you no longer need. If you want to keep it, it must be checked by an engineer registered for gas fires.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="checks">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What does a boiler service include?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">We take the cover off, clean and check the parts inside, and test that the boiler burns gas safely. Here is the full list.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Safety checks</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Flue gas analysis, to prove the boiler burns gas cleanly</li>
            <li>Gas pressure and gas rate checked</li>
            <li>The flue checked along its route, with seals and joints</li>
            <li>A spillage test on older open-flue boilers</li>
            <li>Safety devices tested, so the boiler shuts down if it should</li>
            <li>Air vents checked, as they are often blocked in older homes</li>
            <li>Your carbon monoxide alarm tested, if you have one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Inside the boiler</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Burner and heat exchanger checked and cleaned</li>
            <li>Condensate trap cleaned, and the condensate pipe checked</li>
            <li>Seals and gaskets checked for wear</li>
            <li>System pressure and expansion vessel checked</li>
            <li>Inhibitor level checked and topped up if low</li>
            <li>Magnetic filter cleaned, if you have one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>To finish, we test the heating, hot water and controls. Then we fill in the Benchmark record and email you a copy the same day. Larger homes in Haydock and Newton-le-Willows often have a system boiler. For those, we also check the pump, zone valves and cylinder controls, for the same £95.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does the visit work?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">You book a time, we service the boiler in about an hour, and you get the record by email the same day.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Book (2 minutes).</strong> Call or <a href="/get-started">book online</a>. Tell us the make of boiler if you know it, and if you have a gas fire.</li>
        <li><strong>We arrive.</strong> A Gas Safe registered engineer comes at the agreed time. Anyone can let us in. You can ask to see the Gas Safe card.</li>
        <li><strong>The service (45 to 75 minutes).</strong> We work through the full checklist. We use dust sheets and tidy up after.</li>
        <li><strong>What we found.</strong> We tell you how the boiler is doing. If something needs fixing, you get a price first. You decide.</li>
        <li><strong>Your record.</strong> We fill in the Benchmark record and email you a copy the same day.</li>
        <li><strong>Next year.</strong> We send a free reminder when the next service is due.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Boiler due a service in St Helens?</strong> Call and we will find you the next free slot.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="landlords">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do you do boiler services for St Helens landlords?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Book the boiler service and gas safety certificate (CP12) together for £195. It saves you £20 and one visit for your tenant.</p>
      <p>Renting is growing in St Helens, mainly in WA10 and WA12. By law, landlords must have every gas appliance they supply checked every 12 months. Tenants must get a copy within 28 days. The rules come from the <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/landlords/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safety (Installation and Use) Regulations 1998</a>.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Boiler service</th><th>Gas safety certificate (CP12)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>What it does</strong></td><td>Cleans, tests and sets up the boiler</td><td>Checks every gas appliance is safe</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Needed by law?</strong></td><td>No, but most warranties need it</td><td>Yes, for landlords, every 12 months</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Price</strong></td><td>£95</td><td>£75</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Gas fire in the front room?</strong> If you supply it, it must be on the certificate. We check the boiler, cooker and hob, not gas fires. We can cap the fire so it no longer needs to be on the certificate.</p></div>
      <p>See our <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-st-helens">St Helens gas safety certificate</a> page for more. The <a href="https://www.nrla.org.uk/resources/looking-after-your-property/landlords-gas-safety-responsibilities" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NRLA</a> also has a useful guide.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="warranty">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Will a service keep my boiler warranty valid?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Most boiler makers want a service every 12 months by a Gas Safe registered engineer, written in the Benchmark record. We do both on every visit.</p>
      <p>Your boiler came with a Benchmark checklist, usually in the back of the manual. Each service goes into it. If the boiler breaks down under warranty, the maker can ask to see it. Miss a year and they can refuse a claim.</p>
      <p>No service record at all? We can service the boiler and start a fresh record today. We service all the main makes, including Worcester Bosch, Vaillant, Ideal, Baxi, Glow-worm and Potterton.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="signs">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Does your boiler need a check now?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If you see any of these signs, do not wait for the yearly service. Call us and we will take a look.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>The boiler keeps locking out or showing an error code.</li>
        <li>The pressure keeps dropping, and you keep topping it up.</li>
        <li>Banging, gurgling or kettling noises.</li>
        <li>Black marks or soot around the boiler or gas fire.</li>
        <li>It has been more than 12 months since the last service.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Yellow or orange flame on a boiler or gas fire, or a carbon monoxide alarm going off?</strong> Stop using it, open the windows and get everyone outside. Call the National Gas Emergency Service on <a href="tel:0800111999">0800 111 999</a> first. Then ring us.</p></div>
      <p>If the boiler has stopped working, you need a repair, not a service. Call our <a href="/emergency-plumber-st-helens">emergency plumber in St Helens</a>. Cold spots on radiators? A <a href="/power-flushing-st-helens">power flush</a> may help.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="st-helens">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Where in St Helens do you service boilers?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">The whole borough and the edges of it. The price is the same in every postcode.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Town and central</h3>
          <p>Town centre and Eccleston WA10. Sutton, Thatto Heath and Clock Face WA9. The most Victorian terraces, gas fires and back boilers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Haydock and Rainford</h3>
          <p>Haydock and Rainford WA11, plus Billinge WN5 and Garswood WN4. Mostly post-war homes, with older combis common.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Newton-le-Willows</h3>
          <p>Newton-le-Willows and Earlestown WA12. A mix of Victorian terraces and newer homes with modern combis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
